   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The three national-level Employer and Business Membership Organizations (EBMOs) in Ukraine - the Federation of Employers of Ukraine (FEU), the Association of Employers&apos; Organizations of Ukraine (AEOU), and the Confederation of Employers of Ukraine (CEU) - remain operational but severely affected by the war. Given this context, the ILO&apos;s support will focus on strengthening the EMBOs&apos; services as the most effective way to deliver value to members under the current conditions. The FEU will receive support to diversify its Occupational Safety and Health (OSH) service, with an emphasis on refining its service catalogue and sustainability plan. The FEU will also be supported in establishing an &quot;Industrial Ramstein&quot; - a service to link industrial companies with domestic and international partners and donors, helping to restore their production potential through access to equipment and spare parts at favorable prices. In parallel, the FEU&apos;s affiliated Federation of Metallurgists of Ukraine will develop a service for members aiming to challenge gender stereotypes in mining and facilitate the employment of women in positions traditionally dominated by men. The AEOU will be supported in developing a training and auditing service to help SMEs transition to reliable alternative energy sources, delivered through a Green Energy Help Desk. Its affiliated Association of Employers in the Health Care Sector will also be helped to deliver psychosocial support services to enterprises, with activities covering the development of an Occupational Standard for OSH &amp; Psychosocial Support Specialists, practical workplace guidelines, and examples of good practices. The CEU will be assisted in expanding its consultancy service on employing persons with disabilities (PwD). This will involve the development of a component aimed at assisting companies in creating and effectively implementing internal policies for the post-recruitment integration and retention of PwD.</narrative>
  </description>
